{"title":"2019 Putnam B Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_Putnam_B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let Q be an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />-by-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> real orthogonal matrix,\nand let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/2/6a2d97cd144a2c294cc746bb7513fa2b3dca81d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u\\in\\mathbb{R}^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"15\" /> be a unit column vector (that is, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ec976d7a513fc21a85570a56cbb421d99ba379c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u^\\intercal u=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"15\" />).\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/6/8760e29c3508382441600df367da6b23737ec9e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P = I - 2uu^\\intercal$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"111\" height=\"16\" />, where I is the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />-by-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> identity matrix.\nShow that if 1 is not an eigenvalue of Q, then 1 is an eigenvalue of PQ.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_Putnam_B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We want to show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/0/0b09f04a41729c4378ba1f9f6d701a796f9967d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ-I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> is not invertible. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/a/c3afec5f146839eb4b5c51dc34c29ad670c43c4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P^2=I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"17\" />, this is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/d/4dd540e103248ddd9a39f7cf20540bd848bd6180.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q-P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" /> being not invertible.\n</p><p>From the problem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/2/872a97c24c2264913ad85ebb190dda8f5e43cb2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q-I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"48\" height=\"18\" /> is invertible, so we can use the matrix determinant lemma:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/d/a8dc5d68704df49594a6fe64f2c00f935b475b8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\det(Q-P)=\\det(Q-I+2uu^\\intercal)=(1+2u^\\intercal(Q-I)^{-1}u)\\det(Q-I)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"538\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/e/edeb0835e5b59a514a10bf3c27a8a687ef5d56ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X=(Q-I)^{-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"121\" height=\"21\" />. It suffices to show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/6/8c648de981a9184d438dfe1a507349d3c8c6bba5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+2u^\\intercal Xu=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"122\" height=\"16\" />.\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/4/0f4b566e5dd98e677b36a9236abc7b8082d8f22d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u^\\intercal Xu$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" /> is a scalar (technically a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/8/8a8df7312744a199daa5c8008af5b9b4798bfd64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\times 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" /> matrix), it equals its transpose,\nso <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/3/fc33edc6375d4176b41c44a6c57451c0e96fc487.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2u^\\intercal Xu=u^\\intercal Xu + u^\\intercal X^\\intercal u=u^\\intercal (X+X^\\intercal) u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"337\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/f/82f424cc58483d8783557f7a7d37df397ebc9675.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y=X+X^\\intercal$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"105\" height=\"16\" />. Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/a/eca9c7aeb19370457d85a1b7f54958693a68817d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(Q-I)Y(Q-I)^\\intercal=(Q-I)^\\intercal + (Q-I)=Q+Q^\\intercal-2I.\\]\" width=\"446\" height=\"18\" />\nHowever, we also have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/7/3b7261b23123be2790ec312c4f170c8445f03ab6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(Q-I)(Q-I)^\\intercal=QQ^\\intercal-Q-Q^\\intercal+I=-(Q+Q^\\intercal-2I)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"460\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>If we treat <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> as an unknown variable, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/9/659edb7553b9702fb9ae618df8014b8354f80904.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y=-I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"64\" height=\"16\" /> would be a solution. It is also the only solution, since the map <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/5/7f58413aedc5f0ada71de6d49b9a8d1401c66887.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y\\mapsto (Q-I)Y(Q-I)^\\intercal$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"189\" height=\"20\" /> is injective, due to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/2/872a97c24c2264913ad85ebb190dda8f5e43cb2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q-I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"48\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc9d100c997b9753cef360af5090437f1e477ca2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(Q-I)^\\intercal$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"20\" /> being invertible.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/2/de2e98618de3ac72db8eb1ef6e2be9984c738101.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+2u^\\intercal Xu=1+u^\\intercal Yu=1-u^\\intercal u=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"307\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>~coolcomputery\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_Putnam_B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_Putnam_B_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2019 Putnam B Problems (page does not exist)\">2019 Putnam B Entire Test</a>\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_Putnam_B_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2019 Putnam B Problems/Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">2019 Putnam B Problem 2</a>\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_Putnam_B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2019 Putnam B Problems/Problem 4 (page does not exist)\">2019 Putnam B Problem 4</a>\n</p>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018011429\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.031 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.047 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 144/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 335/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4944/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.894      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n100.00%    5.894      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37379:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018011429 and revision id 288924. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}